# Code owners
#
# These files decide what a human must look at. They are the ones where a
# plausible-looking change could quietly weaken the guarantee this repository
# makes, so they are also the ones the branch protection rule on `main`
# should require a review for.
#
#   site/            the published site — every claim on it is a claim about
#                    this repository
#   .github/         the gates themselves; a weakened gate is the quietest
#                    possible way to make this project look healthy
#   AGENT.md         the activation contract
#   docs/agent/      the same contract, in full
#
# Everything under skills/third-party/ is a byte-identical upstream mirror.
# It must never be hand-edited, so it has no owner by design: changes there
# are wrong by construction, and `validate.py` fails the push regardless of
# who approved it.
