# Governance, carried over from the repository-root CODEOWNERS file.
#
# GitHub uses only one CODEOWNERS file, searching .github/, then root, then
# docs/, and stopping at the first found. Because this file exists, the
# root CODEOWNERS is never read, so the rules below had no effect at all
# until they were copied here. They are the ones where a change would alter
# what an agent is permitted to do, or weaken the gate itself.
#
# skills/third-party/ and skills/catalog/ are deliberately NOT listed: they
# are a byte-identical upstream mirror that must never be hand-edited, so
# they have no owner by design and validate.py fails the push regardless.
